      <outline text="21st November" type="calendarDay" date="2026-11-21">
        <outline text="Kicking the tires. This is nice and it reminds me of something... 🥁" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:24:51 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Listening to The Cakekitchen's [Time Flowing Backwards](https://thecakekitchen.bandcamp.com/album/time-flowing-backwards) after having gone down a Graeme Jefferies rabbit hole while stuck in the Atlanta airport during The Great Ground Stop of 2026. ![The Cakekitchen: Time Flowing Backwards](/images/2026/11/a2894995489-10-21113905.jpg)" created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:26:42 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Camper](https://apps.apple.com/us/app/camper-for-bandcamp/id6822102958) is such a better iOS app for listening to Bandcamp than the Bandcamp app." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 16:29:18 GMT"/>
        <outline text="I took the X100T on the trip to my work conference in Orlando and didn’t use it because I was gonna buy an SD card at a nearby Target, but getting to that Target would have required getting a Lyft/Uber and there was no way I would do that after the harrowing cab ride from the airport to Walt Disney World Dolphin Resort. I don’t know what I was thinking. There wasn’t time to shoot much amidst the conference sessions and having meals with people. So I lugged around a useless camera through the airports. Note to self: Now that I have to carry a CPAP, give up and get rolling luggage." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:01:13 GMT"/>
        <outline text="[Denis Volkov: Task Workflow in Bear Notes](https://medium.com/productivity-heaven/task-workflow-in-bear-notes-517b1fbc4d59) – I never would have thought of putting a date search like `bear://x-callback-url/search?term=2024–04–20` in a Bear daily note, but this is a great idea." created="Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:04:02 GMT"/>
        <outline text="Still playing with Alex's cool new [Porridge](https://github.com/alexjj/porridge) blogging app. My first re-sync of my fork to his is giving me errors. I'm reaching the limits of what I know about GitHub, but it's sort of fun to get in the weeds with." created="Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:42:19 GMT"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </body>
